decisions:
  - id: local-brain-always-on
    decision: Every agent gets an always-on local encrypted brain — learning is the default, upstream flow is the controlled boundary
    rationale: The whole value of renting an agent is that it gets better at YOUR project. Without local learning, every session starts from zero. What's gated is what flows back to the creator/network, not what's learned locally.
  - id: three-deployment-tiers
    decision: Individual (gated upstream), Team (federated brains), Enterprise (all doors open within org)
    rationale: Enterprise agents that learn from all developers in the org create compound intelligence — the real enterprise value prop. Individual users maintain full control over upstream flow.
  - id: four-trust-rings
    decision: project-locked → user-scoped → creator-upstream → network-public with platform enforcement
    rationale: Agents can't circumvent the data policy because denied data never reaches them. The platform filters at the event level, before attention.
