body: |-
  ## Architecture Produced

  ### 1. Agent Manifest (6 new dimensions)
  - **Attention patterns** — continuous relevance filters (vs triggers for dispatch)
  - **Learning protocol** — dual layer: intrinsic (agent-driven) + platform (mandated feedback)
  - **Context contributions** — agents compose CLAUDE.md, not consume it
  - **Work reporting** — structured work log protocol
  - **Collaboration stance** — peer/advisory/supportive/observer with per-agent overrides
  - **Self-nomination** — speak-when and quiet-when rules with relevance thresholds

  ### 2. Ambient Coordination
  - Event stream extracted from tool calls, file edits, conversation
  - Per-agent attention filtering with scoring
  - Nominations (not interruptions) with urgency-based surfacing
  - Debate protocol for conflicting nominations
  - Symphony evolves: ambient + direct + broadcast modes coexist

  ### 3. Lore Split
  - Work Log: auto-recorded, task-structured, project-scoped, ephemeral
  - Learning Journal: agent-private, intrinsic, travels with agent, promotes to notebooks
  - Team Decisions: ADR-style, attributed with participant stances, institutional
  - Backward compatible: existing lore stays, new stream parameter added

  ### 4. Data Sovereignty
  - Four trust rings: project-locked → user-scoped → creator-upstream → network-public
  - **Local brain is always on** — every agent learns locally, encrypted, user owns it
  - Upstream flow is the gated boundary, not local learning
  - Three deployment tiers: individual (gated upstream), team (federated brains), enterprise (all doors open within org)
  - Platform-enforced, not agent-trusted — denied data never reaches the agent
  - Automatic redaction, audit trails, agent-specific overrides

  ## Key Decision
  The local brain reframed the entire trust model. The question isn't "should agents learn?" (always yes, locally). The question is "what flows upstream?" Enterprise value prop: org-wide collective intelligence that compounds across all developers.

  ## Plan File
  Full architecture with YAML examples at: `.claude/plans/twinkling-booping-nest.md`
  Ready for synthesis into formal vision spec in next session.
